Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: caihong: stop requesting continuous splash

Qualcomm ABL's UpdateSplashMemInfo() looks for the exact path
/reserved-memory/splash_region. When it is absent, ABL calls
DisableDisplay() to power down the panel and controller before Linux.
When present, ABL updates the reservation and leaves the display running.

This port does not implement continuous-splash handoff. Drop the splash
reservation, matching the tablets-for-linux Caihong DT. On the Pad 2,
this removes the white/red flash between the bootloader state warning 
and Linux text, including with the earlier backlight, panel and IOMMU 
experiments removed.

Reference: QcomModulePkg/Library/BootLib/UpdateDeviceTree.c

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-oneplus-caihong.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8650-oneplus-caihong.dts
@@ -181,11 +181,6 @@
 			reg = <0x00 0x00 0x00 0x00>;
 		};
 
-		splash_region {
-			label = "cont_splash_region";
-			reg = <0x00 0xd5100000 0x00 0x2b00000>;
-			no-map;
-		};
 	}; 
 
 	/* 4. The Chosen Node (Passing commands to the Kernel) */
